From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kirill <sleeply4cat@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:44:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] net: qrtr: ns: retry announcing services to a new node

qrtr_node_enqueue() refuses everything but HELLO until our own HELLO has
gone out, and that one is sent from delayed work. If the remote's HELLO
reaches the name service first, announcing the local services returns
-EAGAIN and announce_servers() gives up for good.

On SM6225 this leaves the modem without rmtfs and tftp: it stays up with two
services and Wi-Fi never starts, and the only sign is "failed to announce
new service". Retry for up to a second, and print the error if that fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7egg5XM6dMvKwj1kAyq
---
 net/qrtr/ns.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/ns.c b/net/qrtr/ns.c
index bcb090ee7..151de74c2 100644
--- a/net/qrtr/ns.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/ns.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2020, Linaro Ltd.
  */
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/qrtr.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
@@ -218,6 +219,7 @@ static int announce_servers(struct sockaddr_qrtr *sq)
 	struct qrtr_server *srv;
 	struct qrtr_node *node;
 	unsigned long index;
+	int retries = 50;
 	int ret;
 
 	node = node_get(qrtr_ns.local_node);
@@ -226,12 +228,20 @@ static int announce_servers(struct sockaddr_qrtr *sq)
 
 	/* Announce the list of servers registered in this node */
 	xa_for_each(&node->servers, index, srv) {
-		ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv);
+		do {
+			ret = service_announce_new(sq, srv);
+			/* The remote said hello first, ours is still pending */
+			if (ret == -EAGAIN && retries--)
+				msleep(20);
+			else
+				break;
+		} while (1);
+
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			if (ret == -ENODEV)
 				continue;
 
-			pr_err("failed to announce new service\n");
+			pr_err("failed to announce new service: %d\n", ret);
 			return ret;
 		}
 	}
